  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "John B. Rogers was an American businessman whose interests extended across Texas, Louisiana and Florida. Known as Jack, he invested in real estate and served as president and chief executive of Rogers Investment Corporation. The company managed family trusts, and his property investments included substantial bank financing during the 1980s.",
