    "word_count": 50,
    "html": "<p>John B. Rogers was an American businessman whose interests extended across Texas, Louisiana and Florida. Known as Jack, he invested in real estate and served as president and chief executive of Rogers Investment Corporation. The company managed family trusts, and his property investments included substantial bank financing during the 1980s.</p>\r\n"
  },
  "long_biography": {
    "plain_text": "John Burton Rogers spent his childhood in Massachusetts, New York and Florida, beginning his education at Palm Beach Day School. He later attended St. Mark's School in Massachusetts and Yale College. Service in the United States Air Force came before an MBA at Harvard, bringing military experience between his university studies.\n\nAway from business, Rogers travelled widely by sea. His sailing took him through the Caribbean and Mediterranean, along the Gulf of Maine and into the waters of Japan and the Tasman Sea. He and his wife, Alice, were married for more than fifty years.",
    "confidence": {
